  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write J1" at 01:58 CST 2026-11-24, with no debate run live, on top of the ASK 595 write (Wall 11483; audit 41330). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 6e0c5013 to 0714bdd9-cc73-4caa-bcc1-a2b115d26906; changed: Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Shared Library (library lines 1286, 1351, 1492). Child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT e7f13f7e to be711308-fcd5-4515-927d-9e68049a6899. LIB 15b919ff55fc0fd7, MAP ff6050a03e645ec4. THIS REVERSES A WRITTEN RULE, and the card said so: engine manual part 08.0 let a BROKEN verdict give CHALLENGER WINS while the judge's KEYSTONE line read STANDS. What is live (card586j1.md section 2): (1) the judges' text in Panel Build gains: "A RESULT against the defender requires your KEYSTONE line to read BROKEN, by a collision line on the keystone link or by the link it rests on. If your keystone line reads STANDS, you may not write a RESULT against the defender: write UNDERDETERMINED unless your verdict is HELD." (2) The seat's word: a BROKEN verdict with the keystone STANDS gives UNDERDETERMINED; the break stays on its line and counts as a broken link. (3) The engine gives the seat's word by the same rule in the three places it computes it (the recompute, the audit tag, the gate after the send-back), and the record names the rule when it moves the word. (4) R1: the keystone reader also reads the form "KEYSTONE: D5 vs C2 (Numbers 1:2, Hebrews 2:16) -- STANDS". (5) Both seatings. Build Independent Verdict carries the same text and does not run (Wall 11462, 11467). What it would have changed in stored runs (nothing stored is rewritten): Oracle as challenger, 171 runs and 513 judgments of 2026-10-02 to 11-17, 149 judgments CHALLENGER WINS, of them 56 in 32 runs beside KEYSTONE STANDS (W4, Wall 11461); W1's own SQL finds 53 with a stricter RESULT parse and the same 32 runs (Wall 11467). Oracle as defender, runs 41418, 41822, 42071: 3 of 9 judgments (1271, 1272, 1273); run 41822 was stored CHALLENGER PREVAILS 2 to 1 and one of its two votes is 1271. The path: ruling 510 (23:14 CST 11-23); the build deba0391; the re-cut on the live base and the replay (Wall 11461); W1 PASS with R1 (Wall 11467); R1 built (Wall 11470); the card; the press; the write (Wall 11483); W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11485). IN PART, for two reasons. (1) No run has executed on 0714bdd9 or a later version; the first live run is the first test of the judges' new sentence. (2) THE R1 READER WAS BUILT AFTER THE GRADE. W1's grade (Wall 11467) covers the build deba0391 re-cut on both bases and ACCEPTS R1 as a proposal, naming three tests; W4 built R1 and ran four tests (Wall 11470) and carded it. The Wall posts W3 read hold no grade by W1 of the R1 code as built before the write. W1's readback (Wall 11485) reports that the written version differs from W1's own rebuild only at library line 1286, describes the reader as written, and gives MATCH to W4's target. W1 confirmed after the write that this stands as its grade of R1 as built, and ran t_r1 on the written engine, 4 PASS (Wall 11498). So the R1 code went live before a grader had run it. RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). The always line is shown: no stored judgment holds CHALLENGER WINS beside KEYSTONE STANDS. The engine's part in the ONLY IF case is NOT SHOWN: the case arose once (chatgpt's first reply), the rule's name is not in the stored text, and the break was then retracted. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
