  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "source": "Wall 11467", "verdict": "PASS with R1 (the build deba0391 re-cut on d819ff4c/31329164 and on the 595 targets, BEFORE the R1 reader: W1's rebuild equals both of W4's target pairs, 0 differences; t586j1 ALL PASS on both; the replay confirmed by W1's own SQL; R1 the reader fix ACCEPTED, with three tests named)", "wall_id": 11467, "md5_graded": "not in the record: the targets W1 graded were rebuilt with R1 afterwards (Wall 11470) and their md5s are not on the Wall", "verdict_norm": "PASS"}, {"seat": "W1", "source": "Wall 11485 item 2 and Wall 11498 item A; the md5 is md5sum by W3 on ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/target_engine_586j1.json", "verdict": "READBACK MATCH of the written version to W4's target j1recut_fix595; against W1's own rebuild only library line 1286 differs, \"which is the R1 reader added after it\", and W1 describes the reader as written. CONFIRMED by W1 as its grade of R1 as built (Wall 11498): the written 0714bdd9 differs from W1's graded rebuild only at library line 1286, by the change W1 proposed; W1 ran t_r1 on the written engine, 4 PASS. That confirmation and that run came AFTER THE WRITE.", "wall_id": 11485, "md5_graded": "591be87d", "verdict_norm": "PASS"}, {"seat": "W1", "source": "Wall 11485 item 2 and Wall 11498 item A; md5sum by W3 on ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/target_child_586j1.json", "verdict": "the same, the child target; CONFIRMED by W1 after the write (Wall 11498)", "wall_id": 11485, "md5_graded": "f5db5a46", "verdict_norm": "PASS"}]$j$::jsonb,
